# Cartesian (PPP) gantry robot: three orthogonal prismatic axes -- the
# standard "Cartesian manipulator" of the intro chapters (Spong ch. 1).
# With no revolute joints the mass matrix is configuration-independent and
# no trigonometry survives; the generator's symbolic zeros collapse nearly
# the whole computation, making this a good stress test of the folding.

gravity 0 0 -9.81

body                    # 0: bridge carriage, travels along x
parent -1
joint prismatic x
tree 0 0 1
mass 20
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.2 1.5 1.5 0 0 0

body                    # 1: cross carriage, travels along y
parent 0
joint prismatic y
tree 0 0 0
mass 10
cg 0 0 -0.05
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.5 0 0 0

body                    # 2: vertical ram, travels along z; tool force here
parent 1
joint prismatic z
tree 0 0 0
mass 5
cg 0 0 -0.3
inertia 0.4 0.4 0.02 0 0 0
fext 1
